{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-heat-equation-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-heat-equation-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of solutions of the $q$-heat equation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-heat-equation-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-heat-equation-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","q-heat-equation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QHeatEquation.unique_solution","text":"q-heat-equation-unique.md","leanSource":"q-heat-equation-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:q-heat-equation-unique\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Uniqueness of solutions of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation</em></p>\n<p>Given initial data <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u_0</code>, the solution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u(t)</code> of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation is uniquely determined as the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp(-t \\Delta_q) u_0</code> semigroup orbit.</p>\n"}
